{
  "commit": "181b11557eee1e4da74618b06ad3236a324199bf",
  "instructions": "Controls a Batocera retro-gaming cabinet through its EmulationStation frontend: browse systems and games, see what is playing, launch or quit a game, and show messages on screen. While a RetroArch (libretro) game runs, it can also pause, save or load state, take a screenshot, or reset. In the cabinet signal chain, the Batocera PC acts as the Video and Audio Source feeding HDMI into the AV Receiver (Onkyo) or TV (LG webOS). Game launch events automatically trigger dynamic marquee artwork updates on Pixelcade LED marquees. Play session tracking automatically publishes MQTT events to Home Assistant ('batocera/now_playing'). Call batocera_get_status first. To launch a game, find its id with batocera_find_games, then call batocera_launch_game. Only one game runs at a time: batocera_quit_game ends the current one and loses unsaved progress, so confirm with the user before quitting a game someone may be playing.",
  "package": "batocera_mcp",
  "server": "batocera",
